📅 Day 02 – Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC)

🎯 Today's Goal

Understand what Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC) is, why it is important, and learn all its phases with real-world examples.

---

🤔 Why Do We Need SDLC?

Imagine a client asks you to build a School Management App.

If you immediately open VS Code and start coding without understanding the project, you may face many problems:

- ❌ Wrong features
- ❌ Poor planning
- ❌ Wasted time
- ❌ Extra development cost
- ❌ Unhappy client

To avoid these problems, software companies follow a proper development process called Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC).

---

📖 What is SDLC?

Software Development Life Cycle (SDLC) is a structured process used to plan, design, develop, test, deploy, and maintain software.

In simple words,

«SDLC is a roadmap that guides software from an idea to a finished product.»

Instead of randomly writing code, developers follow well-defined steps.

---

🏗️ Real-Life Analogy

Imagine you are building a house.

You don't start by painting the walls.

The correct order is:

- Planning
- Designing
- Building
- Checking
- Handing over
- Maintenance

Software development follows the same idea.

